---
# SKILL.md — Metadata format for relay skills
# Place this frontmatter at the top of your skill's main .md file.
# The manifest scanner (skill-manifest.sh) reads these fields automatically.

# Required fields
name: my-skill                    # Unique slug (lowercase, kebab-case)
description: One-line summary     # What this skill does (keep under 80 chars)
entry_point: ~/relay/skills/my-skill/run.sh   # Path to the executable entry point

# Dependencies — checked by the manifest scanner at build time
# Prefix with config: for relay.conf keys, bin: for binaries in PATH
requires:
  - config:some_api_key           # Checks relay.conf for non-empty value
  - bin:curl                      # Checks command -v curl
  - bin:jq                        # Checks command -v jq

# Trigger phrases — the agent matches these against user messages to self-route
# Keep them short and specific. The agent sees these in the one-line index.
triggers:
  - "do something"
  - "run my skill"
  - "keyword"

# Optional: fallback skill when this one is degraded/unavailable
fallback: other-skill-name

# Optional: captured_from date (auto-populated by skill-capture.sh)
# captured_from: 2026-03-13
---

# My Skill — Full Documentation

Full documentation goes below the frontmatter.
The manifest scanner only reads the YAML block above.
This content is available on-demand when the agent reads the file directly.
